1
00:03:05,454 --> 00:03:11,454
Everyone wants to be found.

2
00:06:10,909 --> 00:06:16,909
Lost in Translation is a drama, romance, comedy film directed by Sofia Coppola.

3
00:09:16,363 --> 00:09:22,363
Two lost souls visiting Tokyo -- the young, neglected wife of a photographer and a washed-up movie star shooting a TV commercial
-- find an odd solace and pensive freedom to be real in each other's company, away from their lives in America.

4
00:12:21,818 --> 00:12:27,818
Bob Harris, played by Bill Murray.

5
00:15:27,272 --> 00:15:33,272
Charlotte, played by Scarlett Johansson.

6
00:18:32,727 --> 00:18:38,727
John, played by Giovanni Ribisi.

7
00:21:38,181 --> 00:21:44,181
Kelly, played by Anna Faris.

8
00:24:43,636 --> 00:24:49,636
Ms. Kawasaki, played by Akiko Takeshita.

9
00:27:49,090 --> 00:27:55,090
Press Agent, played by Kazuyoshi Minamimagoe.

10
00:30:54,545 --> 00:31:00,545
Lost in Translation is a 2003 romantic comedy-drama film
written and directed by Sofia Coppola.

11
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Bill Murray stars as Bob Harris, a fading American movie star who is having a
midlife crisis when he travels to Tokyo to promote Suntory whisky.

12
00:37:05,454 --> 00:37:11,454
He befriends another disillusioned American, Charlotte (Scarlett
Johansson), a recent college graduate and married for two years.

13
00:40:10,909 --> 00:40:16,909
Giovanni Ribisi, Anna Faris, and Fumihiro Hayashi are also featured.

14
00:43:16,363 --> 00:43:22,363
The film explores themes of alienation and disconnection against
a backdrop of cultural displacement in Japan.

15
00:46:21,818 --> 00:46:27,818
It does not use mainstream narrative conventions and is
atypical in its depiction of romance.

16
00:49:27,272 --> 00:49:33,272
Coppola started writing the film after spending time in
Tokyo and becoming fond of the city.

17
00:52:32,727 --> 00:52:38,727
She began forming a story about two characters experiencing a "romantic melancholy" in the Park Hyatt Tokyo,
where she stayed while promoting her first feature film, the 1999 drama The Virgin Suicides.

18
00:55:38,181 --> 00:55:44,181
Coppola envisioned Murray playing the role of Bob from the
beginning and tried to recruit him for months.

19
00:58:43,636 --> 00:58:49,636
While Murray eventually agreed to play the part, he did not sign a contract.

20
01:01:49,090 --> 01:01:55,090
Coppola spent a quarter of the film's $4 million
budget without knowing if he would arrive.

21
01:04:54,545 --> 01:05:00,545
Principal photography began on September 29, 2002, and lasted 27 days.

22
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Coppola kept a flexible schedule during filming with
a small crew and minimal equipment.

23
01:11:05,454 --> 01:11:11,454
The screenplay was short and Coppola allowed
significant improvisation during filming.

24
01:14:10,909 --> 01:14:16,909
The director of photography, Lance Acord, used available light where possible, and many
Japanese places of business and public areas were used as locations.

25
01:17:16,363 --> 01:17:22,363
After 10 weeks of editing, Coppola sold distribution rights for the United States and Canada
to Focus Features, and the company promoted the film through word of mouth.

26
01:20:21,818 --> 01:20:27,818
Lost in Translation premiered on August 29, 2003, at the Telluride Film Festival,
and was distributed to American theatres on September 12, 2003.

27
01:23:27,272 --> 01:23:33,272
It grossed $118 million worldwide and received acclaim for its writing, directing and
performances, though its depiction of Japan and Japanese people was criticized.

28
01:26:32,727 --> 01:26:38,727
At the 76th Academy Awards, Lost in Translation won Coppola Best Original Screenplay, and the
film was nominated for Best Picture, Best Director and Best Actor (Murray).

29
01:29:38,181 --> 01:29:44,181
Other accolades won include three BAFTAs and three Golden Globes.

30
01:32:43,636 --> 01:32:49,636
It has since been named one of the greatest films of the 2000s and 21st century.

31
01:35:49,090 --> 01:35:55,090
The film explores themes of hotel room, adultery,
japan, unsociability, upper class.

32
01:38:54,545 --> 01:39:00,545
The tone is lighthearted and uplifting and emotional.
